        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7de8388e-3643-5cc8-a0ab-627e1917a0c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Son of a Gun (EP), Incesticide, Sliver\n- People: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, Dave Grohl\n- Organizations: The Vaselines, Nirvana, DGC\n- Topics: compilation albums, cover versions, recording sessions, band lineups\n\nFacts:\n- Son of a Gun is the debut EP by the Glasgow alternative rock group The Vaselines.\n- Incesticide is a compilation album by the American grunge band Nirvana.\n- At the time of Incesticide, most of its material was already circulating in fan communities in lower quality.\n- Because Incesticide drew from different recording sessions and from a period when Nirvana lacked a stable lineup, it includes performances by four drummers: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, and Dave Grohl.\n- In 1992, DGC re-released the song \"Sliver\" to radio to support the release of Nirvana's rarities compilation album Incesticide.\n- The title song from Son of a Gun reached a wider audience after Nirvana covered it, along with \"Molly's Lips,\" on the compilation album Incesticide.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "297036f3-11dc-50b7-9f46-0cf3d2341a78",
        "text": "Page: Son of a Gun (EP). Sentence: Son of A Gun is the debut extended play single by Glasgow alternative rock group The Vaselines.\nPage: Son of a Gun (EP). Sentence: The title-song of this EP came to a wider audience after Nirvana covered it, along with \"Molly's Lips\", on their compilation album \"Incesticide\".\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: Incesticide is a compilation album by the American grunge band Nirvana.\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: At the time, the majority of the material on \"Incesticide\" was circulating within fan communities (albeit in lower quality).\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: Since the songs were recorded in different sessions and some were recorded when Nirvana did not have a stable formation, the album includes recordings by four different drummers: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, and Dave Grohl.\nPage: Sliver (song). Sentence: DGC re-released the song to radio to support the release of the rarities compilation album \"Incesticide\" in 1992.",
